        "title": "With your partner",
        "content": {
          "type": "Question",
          "version": 1,
          "locked": false,
          "questionId": "TsX3aw",
          "tiles": [
            {
              "id": "Zs6CVLSzG5rqUIp0",
              "title": "Thinking about your own parallels",
              "fixedPosition": true,
              "content": {
                "type": "Text",
                "format": "html",
                "text": [
                  "<p>Now, you should think about your design.</p><p>What elements of your prosthesis are <u>similar</u>  to a biological hand and arm?</p><p>What elements (if any) were <u>inspired by other things</u> (not a hand and arm) when you designed your prosthesis?</p><p>What elements of your prosthesis are <u>different</u> from a biological hand and arm?</p><p>What elements are <u>missing</u> that would make your prosthesis work like a biological hand and arm?</p><p></p><p>You can write, sketch, or make a table. Choose which tile you want and drag a tile over to answer the question!</p>"
                ]
              }
            },
